tor Pre-College and Summer Youth Programs Inclusion Inclusion Everyone Belongs at the University of New Haven The Myatt Center Accessibility Resources Center Graduate and International Student Life IDEA Council Military & Veteran Affairs Spiritual Life and Campus Ministry Title IX Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends Our Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Involvement Alumni Benefits Magazine Alumni Association Contact Alumni Relations Support the University Research Research Research Overview Labs & Groups Faculty Research Student Fellowships & Research Summer Undergraduate Research Fellowships (SURF) Grants & Sponsored Programs Explore Explore Explore the University West Haven & Beyond News and Media Events Camps and Conferences Community Spotlights The Arts on Campus Digital Downloads Athletics Athletics Social Media Instagram Facebook Tik Tok LinkedIn X YouTube Close Menu Section Menu Student Life / Career Development Center Prospective Students Alumni Employers Main Page Internship Guidelines Recruit Employment Outcomes Staff Frequently Asked Questions for Parents Bergami Internship Close Find Your Organization’s Next Star Employee The University of New Haven’s Career Development Center creates many opportunities for employers from around the state, region, or country to interact with and recruit talented and well-qualified students. Recruit Here Internship Guidelines Job Posting Policies Nationally Recognized Center for Career Development The University of New Haven’s Career Development Center, a comprehensive career planning and employment center for students of all majors and classifications, has been named one of the best in the nation by The Princeton Review . We're On Handshake! The University of New Haven is on Handshake! Gain exclusive access to top-tier talent through Handshake, our innovative platform connecting you with the brightest minds and emerging leaders from our diverse pool of students and alumni. Post internships, part-time roles, and full-time positions tailored to your company's needs. Engage with our vibrant community by attending career fairs, networking events, and workshops designed to foster meaningful connections at the University of New Haven. Join our network of industry leaders and recruiters TODAY! How to Access Handshake Contact Us Career Development Center Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. 103 Bartels Student Activity Center 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 (203) 479-4858 Email Us Online Career Center Take Me to Handshake Upcoming Career Fairs Fall 2025 Wednesday, Sep 10 Day 1 Business, Engineering, Sports, and Entertainment Fair Business, Engineering, Sports, and Entertainment 1 - 4 p.m. | Beckerman Recreation Center Employers Register Here Thursday, Sep 11 Day 2 Healthcare, Science, Criminal Justice, and Non-Profit Fair Healthcare, Science, Criminal Justice, and Non-Profit 1 - 4 p.m. | Beckerman Recreation Center Employers Register Here Spring 2026 Wednesday, Feb 25 Day 1 Business, Engineering, Sports, and Entertainment Fair Business, Engineering, Sports, and Entertainment 1 - 4 p.m. | Beckerman Recreation Center Employers Register Here Thursday, Feb 26 Day 2 Healthcare, Science, Criminal Justice, and Non-Profit Fair Healthcare, Science, Criminal Justice, and Non-Profit 1 - 4 p.m. | Beckerman Recreation Center Employers Register Here Ways to Recruit at the University Online Job and Internship Postings via Handshake Resume Referral Program On-Campus Interviewing & Information Tables Guest Speaker Opportunities Connect with Campus Clubs and Organizations Networking Events with Students & Alumni Access to University’s Alumni Network Job Shadow and Mentoring Opportunities Assistance in Creating a Robust Internship Program Salary Information and Recruiting Trend Data \"The University of New Haven’s Career Development Center takes great pride in partnering with you to support your recruitment efforts to hire the best and brightest and to enhance your involvement with University students, faculty, and administration.\" Matt Caporale, Executive Director, Career Development Center Opportunities to Collaborate Internship Guidelines Recruit Here Job Posting Policies Also of Interest: Student Life - Recruit Our Students -... Career Development Center - University of New Haven Career Development for Prospective Students -... University of New Haven 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 (203) 932-7000 (800) 342-5864 Admissions News and Media Campus Locations and Maps Public Safety Library Employment Give Faculty & Staff Directory Emergency Notifications Strategic Plan Information Technology Support myCharger Alumni Email Title IX Instagram Facebook Tik Tok LinkedIn X YouTube Send Us Feedback Online Privacy Statement Online Accessibility Equal Opportunity and Wrongful Conduct Reporting"
